 "details": {
  "title": "I Get Along Without You Very Well, on the Fret Finder guitar",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, on the bars of the Fret Finder page, which copies the record’s guitar note for note. The notes are the lead sheet’s, in A-flat, the record’s key: concert B-flat 3 to C5 (C to D for the trumpet); each sits where the singer sings it, so the time is hers, very free. The record opens with her own introduction over chords of her own, not the tune: the trumpet rests there and comes in with the song’s first line, slow, in long notes.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Hoagy Carmichael (1939), after a poem by Jane Brown Thompson"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, placed on the singer’s timing from the record"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "A-flat major concert (B-flat for the trumpet)"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Her free introduction (guitar alone here), the song, the last part again, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (igaw-guitar.mp3), 3:22"
   ]
  ]
 }
